# MuxPD TP4 numerical follow-up — preliminary evidence v1

This is a bounded correctness diagnostic on four measured Ascend 910B2 devices,
Qwen3.5-35B-A3B, BF16, TP4/EP4. It is not a throughput, goodput or semantic-quality
result and does not qualify PR #10 for merging. The ten explicitly selected
terminal runs are listed in `terminal-selection-v1.json`; failed attempts remain
included. Pending quality, pressure/cancellation and clean performance experiments
are not inferred from these captures.

## Findings from terminal captures

Normal controls use three repeats of one P128 request and three repeats of four
P128 requests, each with eight greedy output tokens. Full-vocabulary vectors are
saved on rank zero; all four ranks have sampling receipts. The counts below are
paired request sequences and comparable captured rank-zero vectors.

| Comparison | Exact output sequences | Elementwise-equal vectors | Literal equal `.npy` SHA256 |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| Native default-02 warm pairs | 13/15 | 0/88 comparable | 0/88 |
| Native default-03 warm pairs | 13/15 | 0/114 comparable | 0/114 |
| Native default-02 vs default-03 fresh processes | 11/15 | 0/57 comparable | 0/57 |
| Native HCCL=true-01 warm pairs | 15/15 | 120/120 | 120/120 |
| Native HCCL=true-02 warm pairs | 15/15 | 120/120 | 120/120 |
| Native HCCL=true-01 vs true-02 fresh processes | 15/15 | 120/120 | 120/120 |
| Raw HCCL=true extension-01 warm pairs | 15/15 | 120/120 | 120/120 |
| Native HCCL=true-02 vs raw extension-01 | 15/15 | 120/120 | 120/120 |

The last row crosses observer/source revisions and is a descriptive comparison.
Native source `46db71a3e1772c667cc3e235c05eeaf8381f0d43` selects a diagnostic native
worker subclass whose instrumentation is present before native warmup. Raw source
`9f016ff6278c6ca0a6b4d66f08ccff01873c9446` selects the exact production worker plus
a supported extension and installs its observer after warmup. This is not a
single-variable raw/native equivalence experiment. The normal controls use the
default compiler backend; they must not be mixed with the explicit fusion-backend
composite comparison below.

The native-only controls associate the sole explicit
`HCCL_DETERMINISTIC=true` environment change with exact warm/fresh repetition on
this workload. They do not isolate the responsible collective or prove universal
determinism. Native default variability is not a waiver for plugin errors.

The terminal composite native/raw pair uses the same source
`6c606f789450a45ef35afee398b0a3e516caa1a1`, the same post-warmup observer extension,
`HCCL_DETERMINISTIC=true`, and explicit
`enable_npugraph_ex=false, enable_static_kernel=false`. Both use their exact
ordinary worker selectors. Native chunked prefill is enabled; raw complete
prefill uses the plugin and disables chunking, so the algorithm and resulting
batch composition intentionally differ. Each process contains the normal family
followed by a seed-first family; in the staggered four-lane phases the remaining
three P128 requests are admitted when the scheduler records the seed's first
output token.

| Composite comparison | Exact output sequences | Elementwise-equal vectors | Literal equal `.npy` SHA256 |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| Native warm pairs | 30/30 | 240/240 | 240/240 |
| Raw warm pairs | 30/30 | 240/240 | 240/240 |
| Native vs raw | 30/30 | 147/147 comparable | 147/147 |

All 240 output positions agree in this native/raw pair, and all four ranks agree
on sampled token receipts. Only 147 positions pass the analyzer's observed
request-prefix, peer-input and batch matching checks; 93 are not assigned a
same-batch logit-distance claim. Identical current inputs do not prove identical
hidden state or entire process history. The seed-first family shares process
history with the earlier normal family. No group-FX candidate is included in
this v1 selection.

`numerical-summary-v1.json` re-verifies every original analysis input identity and
binds paired vector SHA256 to the sampler receipts. It distinguishes the original
analyzer's historically named `logits_byte_equal` field (elementwise array equality)
from a separate literal `.npy` file-hash comparison. They coincide in the exact
rows above, but their meanings remain separate. Logit distances stop when the
observed request or peer context diverges. The full raw vectors and observations
are retained regardless of whether a comparison is admitted.

## Failures and other bounded evidence

- `native-default-01` failed the original internal/external request-ID verifier
  after one eight-token request; available captures remain archived, with no
  promotion to a complete run.
- `raw-default-01` failed worker-selector contract validation during startup.
  The subsequent extension implementation does not erase this attempt.
- `raw-pressure-geometry-01` completed discovery without requests. It measured
  3,325 native blocks, one full-attention group with 1,024-token blocks and three
  Mamba groups with 16,384-token blocks. Native startup requires 19 blocks and
  the explicit null-block guard requires 20. This is geometry evidence, not
  pressure, preemption, cancellation or reuse evidence.

## Provenance and archive boundaries

Pinned Core is `d0f22d2bda562156e4dbf433ce645e1769b4f804`; pinned Ascend is
`03766ac696fde5ab1980d80ca0b8543d3580c989`. The captured environment reports
torch-npu 2.10.0.post4, and CANN paths identify the 9.1.0 installation. Initial
hardware inventory explicitly names 910B2; the controller records the visible
device selection for each run. Initial model metadata and a subsequent complete
SHA256 inventory of all fourteen safetensors shards are included. Model weights
themselves are not included in these evidence capsules.

Every run directory is archived in full, including failures, process/controller
logs, pre/post device inventories, `.npy` files, all observed ranks, compiler
constants, compiler cache graphs, engine arguments, plans and any locally copied
producer files. Exact source commits are additionally exported with `git archive`,
without Git history; every source-tar file member is independently hashed. These
committed source trees do not reconstruct installed native binary artifacts.

The initial Ascend checkout had an existing `csrc/build_aclnn.sh` modification.
The initial identity records that dirty path. A separately labelled packaging-time
patch/file snapshot is included, but its later hash is not asserted to prove the
exact historical dirty bytes or the compiled binary identity at every earlier
launch. The original evidence is preserved with that provenance limit.

Each capsule embeds its frozen original-member manifest. The builder rechecks
terminal process and process-group status, controller/config/plan identities and
the complete run inventory; verifies compressed output by rereading every member;
and rehashes original inputs afterward. Per-capsule receipts and the versioned
index hash archives and manifests. No active run is inferred from a directory
name, and a missing terminal timestamp/exit code is rejected. Later terminal
runs require new capsules and a new index/report version.

This v1 is local preparation outside the benchmark Git tree. Root still owns
Release upload and subsequent remote download/SHA verification. Local custody
checks are not evidence of remote availability or benchmark acceptance.

## Remaining acceptance work

The same-revision, same-backend raw/group comparison must establish candidate
numerical behavior and group/MoE metadata invariants. The frozen 200-case
MMLU-Pro quality plan still requires two native controls and candidate runs, no
new wrong answers on the native-stable subset, and real mixed execution coverage.
Actual pressure must show the intended D allocation failure and pinned-P
preemption/recovery. Partial/full cancellation must show matching ACK, held-block
ownership, release and reuse. Installed plugin configuration/cleanup checks and
ordinary-worker runs without diagnostic observation must follow. Clean latency,
throughput and goodput measurements are needed before claiming a new benefit.

These observations improve the experimental controls and establish a narrow
native/raw agreement result; they do not yet establish a new throughput/goodput
gain or the value of group-FX compilation.
